      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="introduction">
        <tei:p>In composing this new Birkat haMazon/Blessing After the Meal, I maintained the essential structure of the traditional prayer, which consists of four basic spiritual themes or categories. As with the other new liturgies that I’ve written, I seek here to compose Jewish prayers that express a Diasporist ethic; that is to say, liturgy that views the entire world as our “homeland” and resists the influence of modern political Zionism, which has become so thoroughly enmeshed in contemporary Jewish liturgy.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_43401_introduction"/>
